I've added several important improvements to ensure ports are freed automatically when you stop the server:

1. **Socket Tracking System**: The server now keeps track of all open connections in the `openSockets` object.

2. **Immediate Port Reuse**: Added the `reuseAddress: true` option to allow the server to reuse the address immediately after shutdown.

3. **Socket Cleanup on Shutdown**:
 - All active sockets are now forcibly closed during shutdown
 - This prevents hanging connections that could keep the port tied up

4. **Timeout Safety Mechanism**: If the server doesn't shut down cleanly within 3 seconds, it will force exit.

5. **Proper Signal Handling**: The server now properly responds to both SIGTERM and SIGINT (Ctrl+C) signals.

These changes ensure that:
- When you press Ctrl+C, all connections are properly closed
- When you close the terminal, the server will shut down cleanly
- The port will be freed as soon as possible

To further ensure ports are freed on Windows, you could also add this to your batch file:"}],"tool_calls":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01TrfqcYbnoRta3R2JEyUNKG","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{"target_file": "run-enhanced-server.bat", "instructions": "I'll add a cleanup script to ensure ports are freed when the batch file exits.", "code_edit": "@@ ... @@\necho Starting enhanced server (Ctrl+C to stop)...\necho.\n\nREM Start the server\n\"%PLAYWRIGHT_NODE_EXE%\" \"%SERVER_SCRIPT%\"\n\necho.\necho Server stopped. Press any key to exit...\npause\n@@ ... @@\necho Starting enhanced server (Ctrl+C to stop)...\necho.\n\nREM Start the server with automatic port cleanup\n\"%PLAYWRIGHT_NODE_EXE%\" \"%SERVER_SCRIPT%\"\n\necho.\necho Server stopped.\necho Cleaning up any potentially in-use ports...\nfor /f \"tokens=5\" %%a in ('netstat -ano ^| findstr :%PORT%') do (\n echo Terminating process: %%a\n taskkill /F /PID %%a >nul 2>nul\n)\necho Done.\necho Press any key to exit...\npause"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","name":"edit_file","tool_call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TrfqcYbnoRta3R2JEyUNKG","content":"The apply model made the following changes to the file:

