+# Competitor Analysis Scraper

+A robust backend system for scraping and comparing company data for competitor analysis.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Company Data Scraping**: Automatically collect data about companies from various sources.
+- **Financial Analysis**: Compare financial metrics like market cap, revenue, growth, and profit margins.
+- **Product Comparison**: Compare product offerings, quality, and variety between competitors.
+- **User Metrics**: Analyze customer base, growth, and satisfaction metrics.
+- **Visual Data**: Generate chart-friendly data structures for frontend visualization.
+- **Caching System**: Efficient data caching to minimize repeated scraping and database queries.
+- **RESTful API**: Well-structured endpoints for easy frontend integration.
+
+## Tech Stack
+
+- **Node.js**: JavaScript runtime environment
+- **Express**: Web application framework
+- **MongoDB**: NoSQL database for storing company data and comparisons
+- **Puppeteer**: Headless Chrome for advanced web scraping
+- **Cheerio**: Fast and flexible HTML parsing
+- **Yahoo Finance**: Financial data API integration
+- **Winston**: Logging solution
+- **Node Cache**: In-memory caching
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### Health Check
+
+- `GET /api/health` - Basic health check
+- `GET /api/health/details` - Detailed health check with DB status
+
+### Companies
+
+- `GET /api/companies` - List companies (with pagination)
+- `GET /api/companies/:identifier` - Get company details (by name or ID)
+- `GET /api/companies/search/:term` - Search companies
+- `POST /api/companies` - Create a new company
+- `PUT /api/companies/:id` - Update company data
+- `POST /api/companies/:id/refresh` - Force refresh company data
+
+### Comparisons
+
+- `GET /api/comparison?company1=:name1&company2=:name2` - Compare two companies
+- `GET /api/comparison/recent` - Get recent comparisons
+- `GET /api/comparison/:id` - Get comparison details by ID
+- `GET /api/comparison/detail/:metric` - Get detailed comparison for a specific metric
+- `GET /api/comparison/chart/:type` - Get chart data for visualization
+
+## Setup
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+- Node.js (v14 or later)
+- MongoDB (v4.4 or later)
+- npm or yarn
+
+### Installation
+
+1. Clone the repository
+ ```
+ git clone <repository-url>
+ cd competitor-analysis-scraper
+ ```
+
+2. Install dependencies
+ ```
+ npm install
+ ```
+
+3. Create a `.env` file based on the provided `.env.example`
+ ```
+ cp .env.example .env
+ ```
+
+4. Start MongoDB
+ ```
+ # Using local MongoDB installation
+ mongod --dbpath /path/to/data/directory
+ 
+ # Alternatively, use Docker
+ docker run -d -p 27017:27017 --name mongodb mongo:latest
+ ```
+
+5. Run the application
+ ```
+ # Development mode
+ npm run dev
+ 
+ # Production mode
+ npm start
+ ```
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Comparing Two Companies
+
+```javascript
+// Example: Compare Apple and Microsoft
+GET /api/comparison?company1=Apple&company2=Microsoft
+```
+
+### Fetching Detailed Metrics
+
+```javascript
+// Example: Get detailed financial comparison
+GET /api/comparison/detail/financial?company1=Apple&company2=Microsoft
+```
+
+### Getting Chart Data
+
+```javascript
+// Example: Get user metrics data for charts
+GET /api/comparison/chart/usermetrics?company1=Apple&company2=Microsoft
+```
+
+## Project Structure
+
+```
+├── logs/ # Log files
+├── src/
+│ ├── controllers/ # Request handlers
+│ ├── models/ # Data models
+│ ├── routes/ # API routes
+│ ├── services/ # Business logic
+│ ├── utils/ # Utility functions
+│ └── server.js # Entry point
+├── .env # Environment configuration
+└── package.json # Project metadata
+```
+
+## Data Sources
+
+The system collects data from multiple sources:
+
+- Company websites
+- Wikipedia
+- Financial data from Yahoo Finance
+- Social media presence
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+- Integration with additional data sources
+- Machine learning for sentiment analysis
+- Real-time data updates
+- Enhanced security features
+- Advanced analytics dashboard
+
+## License
+
+[MIT License](LICENSE)
+
+## Contributors
+
+- [Your Name](https://github.com/yourusername) - Initial work
```

